Written: [Self-contained research report](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/detGRH_1/independent_report.md), with proofs, counterexamples, status labels, and literature citations.

Principal findings:

- Multiplicative root selection is impossible when any prime divisor is \(1\bmod4\), even allowing diagonal sign ambiguity.
- The proposed small seeds fail the stated Gauss/shape test.
- Full-rank verified integer relations would yield deterministic subexponential factoring under GRH; obtaining those relations remains open.
- Global field moments do not establish a short explicit hitting list.

[Finite verification checks](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/detGRH_1/verify_report.py) passed.